# Test modules (claude/modules-style-pass.md): top-level items that exist only for the
# tests live in a declared test module, a child module of its own. `Tests` declares a helper
# type with its `derive` and a function over it; `More`, a second test module, names them by
# `use Tests.*`, as a test module may name another's helpers. Neither is read by `prism run`.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
test mod More
use Ui

Add: fn Nat, Nat -> Nat
fn Add a, b = a + b

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label(text=$"{Add 1, 2}")
